From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve caller framebuffer bindings across blur allocation

ProjectM TV-specific fix against projectM v4.1.7 plus patches 0001-0040.
BlurTexture::AllocateTextures calls Framebuffer::SetSize, which unbinds the
read and draw targets on first use and resize. Capture both caller bindings
before allocation so Update restores the actual render targets. Warp shaders
that sample blur update it after warping; losing the target sent subsequent
waveform/border draws to framebuffer zero (error 1286 on headless macOS).

Regression controls cover distinct read/draw targets, first use, unchanged
size, resize, reference-scaled blur, numerical blur output, and the unchanged
midgitstraights of majillaen - featy sweet.milk full renderer.

diff --git a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/BlurTexture.cpp b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/BlurTexture.cpp
--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/BlurTexture.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/BlurTexture.cpp
@@ -114,6 +114,12 @@ void BlurTexture::Update(Renderer::Texture& sourceTexture, const PerFrameContext
         return;
     }

+    // Save caller bindings before AllocateTextures: resizing its framebuffer unbinds both targets.
+    GLint origReadFramebuffer;
+    GLint origDrawFramebuffer;
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER_BINDING, &origReadFramebuffer);
+    glGetIntegerv(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER_BINDING, &origDrawFramebuffer);
+
     // MilkDrop's blur levels are fixed fractions of its texture, blurred by a few of their texels, so
     // their radius is a share of the picture only at one render size. Above the line reference size
     // they are made as from a source of the reference's size (BlurSourceFor()): the blur textures keep
@@ -156,12 +162,6 @@ void BlurTexture::Update(Renderer::Texture& sourceTexture, const PerFrameContext
     scale[2] = 1.0f / (tempMax - tempMin);
     bias[2] = -tempMin * scale[2];

-    // Remember previously bound framebuffer
-    GLint origReadFramebuffer;
-    GLint origDrawFramebuffer;
-    glGetIntegerv(GL_READ_FRAMEBUFFER_BINDING, &origReadFramebuffer);
-    glGetIntegerv(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER_BINDING, &origDrawFramebuffer);
-
     m_blurFramebuffer.Bind(0);

     // Each pass can draw straight into its blur texture instead of drawing into the framebuffer's
